/-
  Actual constructed raw/localized constitutional key transport.

  ## Result

  `buildCanonicalBranchKey_actualTransport` relates the two production compilers at every node
  reachable from the center root:

  * raw: `mol.buildCanonicalBranchKey cap fuel node`; raw success is the *hypothesis*;
  * localized: `input.moleculeGraph.buildOfficialRuleMajorKey
    input.executableOfficialCIPChildren fuel onode`; localized success is *derived*.

  From actual raw success the theorem produces an actual localized key together with
  `ConstitutionalKeyCorresponds rawKey locKey`: equality of the plain Rule-1a projection, Rule-1b
  and Rule-2, and equality of the completeness flag.  The official side is always evaluated on the
  actual executable child enumeration `input.executableOfficialCIPChildren`; no synthetic,
  replacement or reordered enumeration is introduced as a compiler input.

  ## Hypotheses

  The theorem takes, explicitly: `mol.AuthoritativeStructureAgreement input.certified.input`,
  `mol.WellFormed`, `mol.BondRecordsUnique`, covariance of every modelled bond
  (`∀ bond ∈ mol.bonds, bond.kind.IsLocalizedCovalent`), the root history and atom bound,
  `NoOxidoRootEdgeAtRootCopies mol root`, the transparent root identification
  `root = canonicalSelfParentRoot root.atom`, and `NonMancudeGeneratedDuplicates mol root.atom`.
  Reachability and `NodeCorresponds` link each raw node to its official counterpart.  Rule-1a
  plainness on reachable nodes is derived from the accepted
  `GeneratedExactPlainAtomicLabels.reachable_exact_plain_atomic_labels_selfParentRoot`; it is not
  an extra assumption of the transport theorem.

  ## Support infrastructure in this module

  * budget monotonicity (`buildCanonicalBranchKey_mono`, `buildCanonicalChildKeys_mono`);
  * budget independence of the produced key (`buildCanonicalBranchKey_cap_eq`);
  * node-count adequacy of successful keys (`buildCanonicalChildKeys_adequate`,
    `buildCanonicalBranchKey_adequate`, `assembleCanonicalBranchKey_nodeCount`);
  * permutation transport of the budget-threaded child recursion
    (`buildCanonicalChildKeys_swap`, `buildCanonicalChildKeys_perm`);
  * permutation transport of successful sorting and of sorted observables
    (`sort?_isSome_of_perm`, `exists_sort?_of_perm`, `sortCanonicalKeys?_corresponds`);
  * the actual child-enumeration transport
    (`buildCanonicalChildKeys_forall₂_corresponds`, `forall₂_toObservable`).

  ## Permutation obstruction and proof outline

  `OfficialRuleMajorKey.mergeChildren` prefixes every child entry with the child's sorted sibling
  slot, so permuting tied children genuinely changes localized provenance records; full key
  equality is not claimed.  The proof compares only the constitutional observable:

  1. the accepted actual child endpoint gives `Forall₂ NodeCorresponds` between
     `input.executableOfficialCIPChildren onode` and a list that `Perm`-permutes
     `mol.canonicalChildren node`;
  2. the executable/canonical pairs are lifted to canonical order
     (`exists_perm_map_snd_eq`);
  3. the budget-threaded raw child build is moved across the canonical permutation
     (`buildCanonicalChildKeys_perm`), and the fuel induction hypothesis supplies official child
     keys with full correspondence;
  4. the official child result is moved back to the actual executable order
     (`mapM_perm_of_perm`), both official sorts are compared through descending observable
     permutations (`constitutional_observables_eq_of_perm`), and the keys are assembled at the
     observable level (`assemble_columns_of_observable`);
  5. completeness is transported through the sorted permutation (`all_eq_of_perm`).

  ## Scope and preserved distinctions

  * The statement is conditional on actual raw success; it does not prove raw success,
    termination or fuel sufficiency.  Width is not an explicit conclusion, although raw success
    implies `¬ 3 < (mol.canonicalChildren node).length` on nonterminal nodes.
  * Generated multiple-bond and ring duplicates stay admitted; no all-real or all-aromatic gate is
    used.
  * Phantom provenance is excluded structurally (it is not generated by `canonicalChildren`); this
    is proved from reachability, not assumed.
  * Raw provenance records, official source nodes and localized source-tree witnesses are never
    identified.  Only the three constitutional columns and the completeness flag are transported.
  * The P/S oxido first-shell gate is explicit (`NoOxidoRootEdgeAtRootCopies`); no claim is made for
    P/S roots.
  * Source-derived hydrogen/mass data enters only through the existing authoritative-intake
    agreement (`intakeAtomDataCorresponds`).
  * No claim of all-source or public-key equivalence is made and no stereochemical conclusion is
    drawn from this constitutional bridge.

  Every public declaration exported by this module is guarded by `assert_kernel_only`.
-/

import TetraStereo.OneCenter.LocalizedCanonicalRuntimeKeyCorrespondence
import TetraStereo.OneCenter.RawLocalizedChildNodeTransport
